**INTERNATIONAL CAFE    - Upcoming African live music events                                                 [![eventimage](/media/2014/07/eventimage-1.jpg)](/media/2014/07/eventimage-1.jpg)**                                                  You are all invited to come and share and enjoy the everyday life experience of Jamaican music and culture at the International Café, at the Ipswich Masonic Centre on 12 July 2014, where your delicious three course Jamaican meal will be garnished by Calypso music served up by popular and crowd-pleasing Ghanaian-born entertainer JOE TEE. There will be opportunities aplenty for interaction on the night and you are invited, and encouraged, to dance the night away, sing along and shake your booty to JOE TEE’s infectious Calypso and Reggae rhythms. PLEASE NOTE: TICKETS MUST BE PURCHASED IN ADVANCE OF THE EVENT. EVENT DETAILS:

**DATE:**

Saturday 12 July 2014

**TIME:**

From 6.45 P.M.

**VENUE:**

Masonic Centre [Roderick & Nicholas Streets, Ipswich](http://now-events.net/au/place/Roderick%20&%20Nicholas%20streets%20-%20Ipswich)

**TICKET PRICE:**

$ 25.00

**TICKETS AVAILABLE FROM:**

Urban Pantry, 181 Brisbane Street, Ipswich Phone: 0414 703842
